TIP:  If transposing, play the root chord of the transposed (Gadd) and add the 5th not as necessary.

TIP:  For the start of the intro, form (G) and pick the top string and strum, then the 4th string and strum, in an alternating bass rhythm.  Then for (Gadd-) just lift off the 1st string from the preceding (Gadd) for one strum and then right back down again.

TIP:  An alternative opening would be to skip the intro completely and play a single chord strum for each chord throughout the first verse, and then begin a normal cadence strum for the rest of the song beginning with the 1st chorus. 
 
        
